.TH CSTR_RESERVE 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_reserve \- reserve capacity, and call ccol_fatal_err() on failure
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_reserve(s, cap);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro calls cstring_reserve() and then calls ccol_fatal_err() if
cstring_reserve() returns false.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     cstr to change
cap   Minimum number of bytes to reserve (with the null terminator)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro evaluates cap exactly once, so the failure message reports the
capacity that the call used
Call cstring_reserve() directly when you want to handle an error yourself
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_reserve (3)
